A||N||11||bHooper||Lets talk about turn signal stalks...||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||08-21-2000||09:53 AM||||My turn signal/cruise/delayed wiper stalk is showing its age.  Usually once a day, the wipers swish when the turn signal is engaged... unless it is a cool morning, such as today.  Today, the wipers "swished" about a half dozen times on the way into work.<P>Also, the cruise doesnt work at all.  When I first bought the car (1989) the cruise was more of an instant thrust button.<P>What can be done about this?  I understand that the symptoms are usually a result of pinched wireing, either in the stalk or in the column.  Is this a repairable thing, or should I replace the stalk?  If it is repairable, what is the best aproach?  Should  I remove the stalk and solder in new wire's?  What should I expect to pay for a new stalk?<BR>How dificult is it to open up the steering column?... do I need to remove the steering wheel to do this?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||286SE'S||08-21-2000||03:44 PM||||The stalk is not much more than a chunk of plastic. The switches for the cruise are on it but the wiper switch is inside the column. My car does the wiper swipe when turn signals are used. I don't lke the amount of things that can go wrong pulling apart the column so I would try the easy stuff first. I have not done it yet but plan to spray the thing with some contact cleaner when I have the  steering wheel off. It is a packed-in there switch, behind the turnsignal switches. A new stalk may help that swipe too as it seems like it may be hitting the "wash" lever just a bit.<BR>Yikes there is already another thread on this same problem. TerryK says that there is a FIX that involves replacing the motor! Awesome! I have a spare delay motor, much easier to change that.<BR>The cruise control: I would recomend getting a known good one and connect it to the spot under the dash where the old one connects and see if it works. The Helms manual has a good description of this wiring and what the connector looks like. It may save you a lot of frustration if it turns out not to be the stalk. Feeding that wire through the column is a no-fun job.  The control box is mounted opposite the subwoofer amp on the center "hUMp area. That can also be substituted with a known good unit. Hope this info is helpful.<BR>Terry<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 286SE'S (edited 08-21-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||theogre||08-21-2000||03:52 PM||||ALL switches for wipers and cruise are in the stalk. There is a harness that goes from the stalk down the left side of the column to a connector under the dash.<P>I've heard of people changing this w/o removing the steering wheel but I don't know how. The connector is rather large and annoying to get up the column even with the wheel and lock plate off.<P>You can do this yourself. you'll need a steering wheel puller and a lock plate tool. both of which are fairly easy to get.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||08-21-2000||04:43 PM||||I had that wiper sweep problem until it was on all the time. If anyone knows how to change the stalk and where to find a good one please let me know. In the meantime I just added an external switch for the wipers and connected it to the wiper motor fuse circuit. For wipers on I just use that switch and the stalk controls the delay/speed. Not pretty but functional. People ask if that's the nitrous switch  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||08-21-2000||04:49 PM||||To diagnose and fix your cruse control, review this page from the Fiero OnLine Service Guide: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/diag.cruise-control.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/diag.cruise-control.html</A> <P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000005||Rodney||08-21-2000||05:52 PM||||I have import replacement cruise stalks. $45 each. Looks just like the real thing. For those with good stalks but the lettering is worn I have stickers to put on to make it look like new again. Stickers will be on my web page soon. Stickers are $4.00 for a 2 part sticker. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||08-21-2000||08:58 PM||||Rodney, do your stalks include delay wipers?||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||08-21-2000||10:13 PM||||good question... delay wipers.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rodney||08-21-2000||11:40 PM||||I have both delay and non delay. Non delay with cruise is a very rare option. ||||reg||1
